{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90476517e1bad9a0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Distributed Workloads\n2\t\n3\t**Jira component**: Distributed Workloads\n4\t**Maturity**: Stable (GA); topology-aware scheduling Tech Preview\n5\t**Owning team**: Distributed Workloads\n6\t**Upstream**: kubernetes-sigs/kueue, project-codeflare/codeflare-operator, ray-project/kuberay\n7\t**Midstream**: opendatahub-io/kueue, opendatahub-io/codeflare-operator, opendatahub-io/kuberay\n8\t**Konflux onboarded**: yes\n9\t\n10\t## Role in the platform\n11\t\n12\tQueueing and orchestration layer for batch AI workloads. Kueue is the platform's\n13\tqueueing system (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model, all-or-nothing admission\n14\tvia waitForPodsReady); Volcano is not shipped or supported. KubeRay manages Ray\n15\tclusters; CodeFlare SDK is the user-facing entry point for Ray-based jobs.\n16\t\n17\t## Dependencies\n18\t\n19\t- cert-manager for Kueue webhooks\n20\t- NVIDIA GPU Operator for GPU resource discovery and time-slicing configuration\n21\t\n22\t## Interfaces\n23\t\n24\t- ClusterQueue, LocalQueue, Workload CRDs (kueue.x-k8s.io)\n25\t- RayCluster/RayJob CRDs (ray.io); PyTorchJob admission via Kueue integration\n26\t- Kueue metrics (pending/admitted workloads per queue) exposed to Prometheus\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a65db390099a467f","agent_id":"a394a185cba9bf004","session_id":"93310d5d-28f6-44a7-9cad-8975610828da","uuid":"0f1b9df6-9975-495b-9428-53ffbcc1a9a2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:06:43.974Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-90476517e1bad9a0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
