mption for selectable time ranges, sourced from the report API.\n- Current-month consumption displayed against each project's Kueue quota (quota figures reconcile with Kueue LocalQueue/ClusterQueue quota — validation of the passive DW side).\n- CSV export accessible from the admin view.\n- Admin view gated to platform administrators (RBAC)? Dashboard uses OpenShift OAuth project-scoped RBAC; admin view needs admin role. Reasonable AC: \"The chargeback admin view is accessible only to platform administrators\" — derived from \"administrator-facing\". OK.\n- Build green in odh-dashboard pipeline.\n\nE004 ACs:\n- Doc topics published covering report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour, per the consumption contract) and export integration (API + CSV usage for finance tooling).\n- Technically reviewed against the implemented reporting capability (Rule 24).\n\nNow signal rationale files: artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001-ai-signals.md ... E004. One per epic (E001 uses investigation_signals).\n\nFrontmatter: need to check schema. Let me run `python3 scripts/frontmatter.py schema epic-task` and `schema decomp-review`/strat... Also check the decomposition summary schema — the summary file gets frontmatter parent_strat, epic_count, critical_path_length, triage... wait, triage fields only for triaged strategies. This strategy is NOT triaged (proceeds to full decomposition), so no triage field. Actually \"Add triage=<value> triage_rationale for triaged strategies (Step 0)\" — not applicable here. Hmm, but should I add triage=full? Only for triaged. Skip.\n\nLet me check the schemas and the validator script to make sure I comply. Also check pipeline-state (tmp/pipeline-state.yaml) — the CLAUDE.md mentions pipeline execution constraints with wait-for-wave, but that's for the parent orchestrator launching waves of agents. I'm the decompose agent; my final action is setting decompose_complete=true. The wait-for-wave constraint applies \"after launching each wave of agents\"