 | |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | New documentation topics (report semantics, export integration) — substantive content authoring, so a separate docs-authoring epic. Priority P1 per the docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Major → P1). |\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n  Teams table, no per-component change/owner detail (Affected Components is a\n  bare list), no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n  and no Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were inferred from architecture\n  context (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard; Distributed Workloads → Distributed\n  Workloads); epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs.\n- **External timing risk** (strategy open question): the metering data schema\n  finalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands. The timing is externally\n  controlled and cannot be compressed; it is recorded as a risk on the report\n  backend epic, not as an acceptance criterion.\n- **Non-obvious component mapping**: the report computation backend is\n  assigned to Distributed Workloads. The strategy lists only Dashboard and\n  Distributed Workloads as affected, and per `dashboard.md` the Dashboard owns\n  no data plane and exposes no private component APIs, so backend-side\n  reporting work maps to Distributed Workloads — the component whose stack\n  runs the metered GPU workloads and owns the Kueue quota model.\n- **Distributed Workloads is passive for HLR-3**: per-project Kueue quota is\n  readable from the existing Kueue CRDs, so no Distributed Workloads code\n  change is needed for the quota side; its validation is an acceptance\n  criterion on the Dashboard view epic.\n- **Bundled P1 HLRs**: HLR-2 and HLR-3 are P1 but bundled into P0 epics on\n  shared surfaces — the inline rationale is in the traceability matrix rows\n  above.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nEvaluated per Rule 18 / Step 5.5: the external dependency (metering data\nschema, uncertain timing) gates every user-facing deliverable — reports, the\nquota-vs-consumption view, and exports all compute from the metering data, and\na quota-only view has no independent chargeback value. No partial-value tier\nexists beyond the risk-reduction investigation itself, so delivery is linear:\nthe consumption-contract investigation proceeds first, and the report backend,\nDashboard view, and documentation follow. The metering dependency is modeled\nas a precondition (Rule 21 — the third party resolves it), with the timing\nrisk noted in Health Warnings.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37360,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a65db390099a467f","agent_id":"a394a185cba9bf004","session_id":"93310d5d-28f6-44a7-9cad-8975610828da","uuid":"363f6576-417d-4b27-9436-657a15a8b680","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:12:02.202Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
