over\n50\t  selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data according to the\n51\t  agreed consumption contract (fields, attribution semantics, time-range\n52\t  semantics).\n53\t- A stable, versioned, documented API for retrieving per-project GPU-hour\n54\t  reports, suitable for finance tooling integration.\n55\t- CSV export of reports through the same API.\n56\t- Reconciliation checks that computed report figures match the source metering\n57\t  data.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given sample metering data, per-project GPU-hour reports compute correctly\n62\t  over selectable time ranges and reconcile with the source metering data.\n63\t- Reports are retrievable through a documented, versioned API suitable for\n64\t  finance tooling.\n65\t- Reports are exportable as CSV via the API.\n66\t- Changes build and pass tests in the component's existing Konflux pipeline.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n71\t  ranges, computed from the metering data.\n72\t- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and the stable finance API share the same\n73\t  report-delivery surface as HLR-1's report computation — a split would build\n74\t  the same service and endpoints twice, so the export capability ships with\n75\t  the report service.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- The metering data schema finalizes only when the metering strategy\n80\t  (RHAISTRAT-9990) lands; that timing is externally controlled and cannot be\n81\t  compressed. This is a precondition recorded as a risk, not an acceptance\n82\t  criterion — the mitigation (direct consumption vs. an isolation layer) is\n83\t  decided by the metering data consumption contract investigation.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9927b2a906084768","agent_id":"a5d3bd03a73995913","session_id":"93310d5d-28f6-44a7-9cad-8975610828da","uuid":"752bb7b2-05b8-4a60-abb8-f8cb57fcb697","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:14:01.294Z","t