{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-895e84e9dce821c1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Metering data consumption contract for GPU chargeback reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Metering data consumption contract for GPU chargeback reporting\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's open question: how GPU chargeback reporting consumes\n30\tthe per-project GPU-hour metering data being delivered by the in-flight GPU\n31\tusage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), whose data schema is not final until\n32\tthat strategy lands. This investigation defines the consumption contract —\n33\tschema, access method, and attribution semantics — and decides whether the\n34\treport implementation consumes the metering data directly or behind a\n35\tschema-isolation layer. The report computation backend's data-access design\n36\tdepends on this outcome.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Determine the metering data schema as drafted and as planned to land:\n41\t  fields, per-project attribution, and GPU-hour semantics (what counts as a\n42\t  GPU-hour for a project).\n43\t- Determine the access method and time-range query semantics for report\n44\t  computation (how reporting reads the metered usage data).\n45\t- Assess schema stability and decide: consume the schema directly, or build\n46\t  the report computation behind an isolation/adapter layer so later schema\n47\t  changes do not rewrite the reporting surface.\n48\t- Agree the consumption contract with the owners of the metering strategy and\n49\t  record a stability verdict with the criteria used.\n50\t- Write down the downstream consequences if the schema changes after the\n51\t  metering strategy lands (what would need to change in report computation).\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A written consumption contract exists that defines the metering data fields\n56\t  consumed, the per-project GPU-hour attribution semantics, and the time-range\n57\t  query semantics for reporting.\n58\t- A stability verdict is recorded (consume directly vs. behind an isolation\n59\t  layer) together with the criteria used to decide it.\n60\t- The consumption contract is recorded as reviewed by the owners of the\n61\t  metering data strategy.\n62\t- The consequences of post-landing schema changes for the report computation\n63\t  are documented (which parts of the reporting implementation would change).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-1 (P0): establishes how per-project GPU-hour data is consumed for\n68\t  reporting — prerequisite to computing the reports HLR-1 requires.\n69\t- Resolves the strategy's Open Question 1 (metering schema finalization and\n70\t  external timing risk).\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4323ccb0522a253","agent_id":"a703a1e8fc5574bf6","session_id":"93310d5d-28f6-44a7-9cad-8975610828da","uuid":"1af78665-9786-47fe-8414-71f0c1de6a33","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:21:26.335Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-895e84e9dce821c1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
