{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ea92c5a9e0ee6c0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Per-project GPU-hour report computation backend with stable API and CSV export\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the metering schema is still in flux when the contract is\n15\t    agreed, the report computation is built behind a schema-isolation layer against\n16\t    the draft contract and realigned when the metering strategy lands; if metering\n17\t    delivery slips indefinitely, this epic slips with it and only the consumption\n18\t    contract stands.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 0\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Per-project GPU-hour report computation backend with stable API and CSV export\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tDelivers the reporting backend for GPU chargeback: computation of per-project\n41\tGPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges from the metering\n42\tdata delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy, exposed through a stable\n43\tAPI for finance tooling and exportable as CSV. This epic does not re-implement\n44\tmetering collection — it consumes the metering data per the agreed consumption\n45\tcontract.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Report computation: per-project GPU-hour consumption aggregated over\n50\t  selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data according to the\n51\t  agreed consumption contract (fields, attribution semantics, time-range\n52\t  semantics).\n53\t- A stable, versioned, documented API for retrieving per-project GPU-hour\n54\t  reports, suitable for finance tooling integration.\n55\t- Exposure of the report API to the Dashboard: per the Dashboard's\n56\t  architecture (Kubernetes API only, no private component APIs), the report\n57\t  surface the Dashboard consumes must be Kubernetes-API-compatible. The\n58\t  concrete exposure mechanism — a CR-backed report surface, an aggregated\n59\t  API, or a Dashboard-backend proxy — is an open design point to be settled\n60\t  in this epic's API design and documented alongside the API.\n61\t- CSV export of reports through the same API.\n62\t- Reconciliation checks that computed report figures match the source metering\n63\t  data.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- Given sample metering data, per-project GPU-hour reports compute correctly\n68\t  over selectable time ranges and reconcile with the source metering data.\n69\t- Reports are retrievable through a documented, versioned API suitable for\n70\t  finance tooling.\n71\t- Reports are exportable as CSV via the API.\n72\t- Changes build and pass tests in the component's existing Konflux pipeline.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n77\t  ranges, computed from the metering data.\n78\t- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and the stable finance API share the same\n79\t  report-delivery surface as HLR-1's report computation — a split would build\n80\t  the same service and endpoints twice, so the export capability ships with\n81\t  the report service.\n82\t\n83\t## Risks / Notes\n84\t\n85\t- The metering data schema finalizes only when the metering strategy\n86\t  (RHAISTRAT-9990) lands; that timing is externally controlled and cannot be\n87\t  compressed. This is a precondition recorded as a risk, not an acceptance\n88\t  criterion — the mitigation (direct consumption vs. an isolation layer) is\n89\t  decided by the metering data consumption contract investigation.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4323ccb0522a253","agent_id":"a703a1e8fc5574bf6","session_id":"93310d5d-28f6-44a7-9cad-8975610828da","uuid":"bf72d695-3398-489a-9d45-bbe2826282c2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:21:26.936Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ea92c5a9e0ee6c0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
