y out of scope: metering collection internals and any\n53\t  currency/cost-rate modeling (reports are in GPU-hours, not dollars).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Published documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a\n58\t  GPU-hour and how per-project attribution works) and export integration\n59\t  (API retrieval and CSV export for finance tooling).\n60\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented reporting\n61\t  capability and administrator view.\n62\t- The content follows the Red Hat docs content process for authoring and\n63\t  publication.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a\n68\t  GPU-hour) and export integration.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4323ccb0522a253","agent_id":"a703a1e8fc5574bf6","session_id":"93310d5d-28f6-44a7-9cad-8975610828da","uuid":"74a882fc-cb03-4337-9cd9-558e64084685","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:21:28.563Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d29078e51558f12","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
